<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n109518" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποφόν-ια</span></b> , τά, at
		Athens, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>price paid by the
				murderer</i> to the relations of the deceased, to buy off their
			vengeance, <i>were-geld,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Din.
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				<u>Frr.</u>
				10.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				18.11
			</span></i>) et <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Harp.
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καταθεὶς τὰ ὑ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.Jun.
					<u>Im.</u>
					10.8
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Aristid.
				2.436J.
			</span></i>: metaph., <i>blood-money,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. τοῖς στρατιώταις ἐδεδώκει τῆς
					σφαγῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					77.12
				</span></i>
			.</div>
